==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From late {{inh|is|non|enginn}}, from earlier {{m|non|engi}}, {{m|non|eingi}}, the ending {{m|non|-inn}} taken from adjectives. Similarly, the neuter {{m|is|ekkert}} is from earlier {{m|non|ekki|gloss=nothing}} by analogy with {{m|is|hvert|gloss=each|pos=neuter}} {{m|non||E(i)ngi}} is a fusion of {{m|non|einn|gloss=one}} + {{m|non|-gi|gloss=not}}.

